This is Speedy MIDI version 1.1, a stable release of the 
"Speedy Rehearsal MIDI Creator" by Holger Hoffmann.


INSTALLING Speedy MIDI

On Windows, simply use the installer executable to install the 
binaries and examples. The source code is distributed as a separate ZIP-file.

To compile the source code, follow the instructions in the INSTALL file.

The source code should work on Windows XP/Vista/7 and Linux (tested on 
Ubuntu 10.04). Since I have no Mac available, I could not compile on a Mac.
This is a future project.


DEMOS AND EXAMPLES

See introduction.txt for a basic introduction to Speedy MIDI.

Once Speedy MIDI is installed, load a MIDI file from the examples directory,
or any other MIDI file you want. Take a look at the functionality of the
editor and MIDI playback.


MIDI PLAYBACK ON LINUX

Speedy MIDI uses the ALSA MIDI sequencer interface.

I installed the following packets for software MIDI synthesis:
timidity, eawpatches

Then run timidity from the console:
timidity -iA -B2,8 -Os1l -s 44100

or add the following line to /etc/init.d
TIM_ALSASEQ=true

For software-synthesized MIDI on Ubuntu, also see:
https://help.ubuntu.com/community/Midi/SoftwareSynthesisHowTo?action=show&redirect=MidiSoftwareSynthesisHowTo


DOCUMENTATION

Currently there is no documentation, unfortunately. The program should be 
self-explaining in most cases. If not, ask in the forum. 


HOW TO REPORT A BUG

Bug reports to: http://sourceforge.net/projects/speedymidi/support

Always include the following information in your bug report:
- Speedy MIDI version
- Qt version
- Compiler name and version
- OS name and version

Remember, this is a spare time project.


